HumMod / Chlorothiazide

Created : 02-Feb-2025
Last Modified : ---
Author : Tiffany 
Copyright : 2006-2010
By : University Of Mississippi Medical Center
Schema : DES V1.0


<!-- Simulates hepatic clearance of ethanol into acetaldehyde and acetate:

Ethanol converted to Acetaldehyde (via alcohol dehydrogenase, ALCDH)
Acetaldehyde converted to Acetate (via aldehyde dehydrogenase, ALDH) -->


<structure><name> EthanolLiver </name>

<variables>

<var><name> Loss </name></var>
<var><name> LossToAcetaldehyde </name></var>
<var><name> TransferToALDH </name></var>
<var><name> [Acetaldehyde] </name></var>
<var><name> [Acetate] </name></var>
<var><name> LossToAcetate </name></var>
<var><name> GainAcetaldehyde </name></var>
<var><name> GainAcetate </name></var>
<var><name> LossAcetaldehyde </name></var>
<!-- <var><name> ALDH2_Activity </name></var> -->

<parm><name> ALCDH_K </name><val> 0.003 </val></parm> <!-- Rate constant for alcohol dehydrogenase (ethanol → acetaldehyde) -->
<parm> <name> ALDH_K </name><val> 0.0167 </val></parm> <!-- Rate constant for acetaldehyde (aldehyde) dehydrogenase (acetaldehyde → acetate) -->

<!-- Asian Flush Parameters
<parm><name> ALDH2_ResidualFraction </name><val> 0.10 </val></parm> <!-- minimum residual ALDH2 activity (fraction of normal) -->

<call> EthnicityChange </call>

<def><name> InitialMass </name><val> TargetConc * ECFV.InitialVol(L) </val></def>
<def><name> Mass </name><val> InitialMass </val></def>

</block>

<block><name>EthnicityChange</name>

  <!-- Replicate this for ALDH -->
<def><name> Asian </name><val> 1.08 </val></def> 
<def><name> Black </name><val> 1.03 </val></def> 
<def><name> White </name><val> 1.00 </val></def>
<def><name> Hispanic </name><val> 0.993 </val></def>
<def><name> TargetConc </name>
  <val> TargetConc
    + ( Context-Ethnicity.TrueAsian_Percentage / 100 * AsianT ) 
    + ( Context-Ethnicity.TrueBlack_Percentage / 100 * BlackT )
    + ( Context-Ethnicity.TrueWhite_Percentage / 100 * WhiteT )
    + ( Context-Ethnicity.TrueHispanic_Percentage / 100 * HispanicT )
    - 1 <!-- This substraction accounts for how the default value leads to a +1 addition here -->
  </val>
</def>

<!-- Ethnicity-specific default deficiency fractions (0..1). Tweak these to change how strongly each ethnicity contributes) -->
<parm><name> ALDH2_Asian_DefFrac </name><val> 0.50 </val></parm> 
<parm><name> ALDH2_Black_DefFrac </name><val> 0.02 </val></parm>
<parm><name> ALDH2_White_DefFrac </name><val> 0.01 </val></parm>
<parm><name> ALDH2_Hispanic_DefFrac </name><val> 0.08 </val></parm>

<!-- Setup as value of deficiency determined by ethnicity (do in this file refer to testosterone) -->

<!--ALDH Deficiency (%) parameters
0% → normal enzyme (no flush)
50–60% → heterozygous deficiency (moderate flush)
100% → homozygous deficiency (severe flush) --> 

</variables>

<equations>

<diffeq>
  <name> MassAcetaldehyde </name> <!-- Amount of acetaldehyde currently in the liver pool-->
  <integralname> MassAcetaldehyde </integralname>
  <initialval> 0.0 </initialval>
  <dervname> ChangeAcetaldehyde </dervname>
  <errorlim> 1.0 </errorlim>
</diffeq>

<diffeq>
  <name> MassAcetate </name> <!-- Amount of acetate currently in the liver pool-->
  <integralname> MassAcetate </integralname>
  <initialval> 0.0 </initialval>
  <dervname> ChangeAcetate </dervname>
  <errorlim> 1.0 </errorlim>
</diffeq>

</equations>

<definitions>

<block><name> Dervs </name>

<def>
  <name> GainAcetaldehyde </name> 
  <val> ALCDH_K * EthanolPool.[Ethanol] * HepaticVein.PlasmaFlow / 1000 </val> 
  </def>
  <!-- Multiplying Ethanol concentration × flow gives grams of ethanol delivered to the liver per minute. 
   Mulipty by ALCDH rate constant (fraction of ethanol metabolized by ALCDH) and / by 1000 to convert ml to L  -->

<def>
  <name> Loss </name>
  <val> GainAcetaldehyde </val>
</def>

<def>
  <name> LossAcetaldehyde </name>
  <val> ( ALDH_K * ALDH2_Activity * MassAcetaldehyde ) + 0.1 </val>
  <!-- Mulipty ALDH rate constant (fraction of acetaldehyde converted to acetate) by total amount 
   of acetaldehyde in the liver pool (grams) for rate of acetaldehyde removal -->
</def>

<!--
ASIAN FLUSH
<def>
  <name> ALDH2_Activity </name>
  <val> 1.0 - ALDH2_Deficiency(%) / 100.0 </val>
</def>

ALDH2 enzyme activity fraction (ALDH2 deficiency affect acetaldehyde clearance)
Translates deficiency percentage into a remaining enzyme activity fraction.
Starts from full activity (1.0)
Reduces proportionally to ALDH2_Deficiency(%)
But can never drop below the ALDH2_ResidualFraction --> 

<!--
Scaled rate constant for ALDH2 metabolism
Clearance of acetaldehyde depends on the current enzyme activity fraction.
If ALDH2_Activity = 1.0 → normal clearance (no flush).
If ALDH2_Activity = 0.5 → half the normal clearance → acetaldehyde accumulates.
If ALDH2_Activity = 0.1 → only 10% clearance → large buildup → red flush and
--> 

<def>
  <name> GainAcetate </name>
  <val> LossAcetaldehyde </val>
</def>

<def>
  <name> ChangeAcetaldehyde </name> <!-- Acetaldehyde changes: production minus clearance -->
  <val> GainAcetaldehyde - LossAcetaldehyde </val>
</def>

<def>
  <name> ChangeAcetate </name>
  <val> GainAcetate </val> 
</def>

</block>

</definitions>

</structure>

End